From 445b14484cc0d41a48f1ce0a4d5577dc83627ebe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: warelik <warelik@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:32:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Accept Codex custom tools and hosted search on the Muse
 Responses lane

Codex declares the capabilities of the built-in OpenAI model it was
configured from, so every routed model receives a freeform `custom`
apply_patch tool and a web_search tool carrying
search_content_types ["text","image"]. Meta's Responses executor
rejects both before the first token: search_content_types is accepted
on no tool shape (web_search_preview included), and `custom` tools
are not supported at all. Every Codex turn against a Muse model
failed with one of those 400s, main turns on the search field and
title-generation turns on the custom tool.

For the Muse Responses lane, strip search_content_types from tool
declarations and send custom tools as ordinary functions with one
raw `input` string, the same shape the Responses->Chat translator
uses: declarations (including namespaced children and
additional_tools), history calls and outputs, and tool_choice. The
converted identities ride _customToolNames under their wire names
(post-cloaking), and every response path presents the calls back as
custom_tool_call with the unwrapped input: non-streaming JSON, the
forced SSE->JSON conversion, and the streaming passthrough, where
function argument fragments are buffered and emitted once as
custom_tool_call_input delta+done. Ordinary function calls and all
non-Muse passthrough traffic are unchanged.
